>The only scaring method available in the early game is the
>dust Elbereth: unreliable and ineffective against a significant class of
>monsters (@).

  In initial game Elberething early and often is sufficient.  Hostile @s
don't regularly show up until much later.  Using Elbereth early and
often on other monsters will leave more cushion for Elbereth resisters.

  By the time hostile @s start showing up regularly other means of
scaring are likely to be found:

  - mirror
  - tooled horn
  - leather drum
  - drum of earthquake
  - Scroll of scare monster.
    - A blessed ?oScareMonster can be written once identified.
    - Drop it, rebless when pick it up.
    - Even works on:
      - the Plane of Air.
      - Bubbles on the Plane of Water.


  NB: tooled horn and leather drum scare Air Elementals that are
engulfing your character.  You will be spat out and the Air Elemental
will flee.  Wizmode tested on the Plane of Air.

  Throwing daggers early and often will make a cushion for dealing with
Elbereth resisting monsters.

